From 934f055419e3d9e7f9daa2b12263b37d615df7af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:41:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Requeue an exhausted-resend owner stall
 (worker_receipt_timeout / owner_link_closed) without charging the card

Sibling of #2658 (owner_unavailable). When the resend's redial reaches the gateway but send 2/2
still gets no receipt, or the owner drops the link again, RuntimeSessionStore._persist_resending
latched WorkerPersistenceError(str(exc)). The bound worker then died with
"Worker failed: WorkerPersistenceError: worker_receipt_timeout" (or a raw ConnectionClosed /
ConnectionError text), which kanban_owner_storage_refusal._KINDS did not match, so the run was
booked crashed and charged to the card.

Five whys
1. Why was the card charged? The terminal envelope was not in _KINDS.
2. Why not? #2658 only added owner_unavailable (redial found no discovery answer).
3. Why does the sibling path give another envelope? The final resend latches the raw exception
   text: worker_receipt_timeout is fixed, but link-closed text carries owner-chosen close reasons
   and errno strings, so no whole-line match could cover it.
4. Fix: the store latches a fixed wire code at the raise site (exhausted_resend_code):
   worker_receipt_timeout for a silent owner, owner_link_closed for a dropped socket,
   ConnectionError, or an owner close code that means the owner went away/failed
   (1001/1006/1011/1012/1013). Any other close code (1009 too big, 1008 policy, 1000) may answer
   THIS frame, so its raw text is kept and the card still owns it.
5. Both codes map to OWNER_UNREACHABLE; whole-line exactness and the NEUTRAL_STREAK_LIMIT breaker
   are unchanged, and the run error names the code.

Proof
- RED on base (source reverted, tests kept): 17 failed, incl. the two-receipt dispatcher replay
  for both envelopes and their breaker streak. GREEN: 466 passed across 52 test files that import
  runtime_session_store / kanban_owner_storage_refusal / kanban_host_refusal;
  test_kanban_owner_unreachable_midrun.py stays green.
- Replay over the hub's real rows (kanban.db, boards/*, sync-shadow/*, read-only): every
  "WorkerPersistenceError: worker_receipt_timeout" receipt is exit 1 and clusters in owner-stall
  bursts: 11 cards within 15 s at 2026-10-31 00:10Z, 6 cards within 18 s at 2026-11-11 15:55Z
  (incl. example-tools t_01a197166756bd53 run 183, the card of #2658's incident), plus 2 on bb.
  All were booked crashed/charged; with this change they requeue neutrally. No receipt carries
  raw ConnectionClosed/ConnectionError text. ENOSPC and invalid_params receipts still count.
